* Built an HNSW vector database from scratch in C++17 (AVX2/FMA kernels, metadata-filtered search, CRC32 atomic persistence, pybind11 bindings, FastAPI and CLI) with {n_cpp} C++ test suites and {n_py} Python tests; on Fashion-MNIST (60K x 784) it reaches {fm_recall50} recall@10 at ef=50 with p50 {fm_p50} ms, in line with FAISS and hnswlib at the same parameters.
* Ran a 25-seed construction study on tightly clustered data that traced a recall gap to the original construction defaults, raising mean recall@10 from {legacy_recall_mean} to {cured_recall_mean} (worst seed from {legacy_recall_min} to {cured_recall_min}) and cutting mean 1-NN self-retrieval failures from {legacy_unreach_mean} to {cured_unreach_mean}.
* Built a generated-docs pipeline in which every published benchmark number is rendered from raw run JSON, with checkers that fail on hand-edited tables, banned claims, and changed targets ({n_targets} targets frozen in git).

